    "result_text": "Full suite is green. \n\nThe full test run shows only one test class exists (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nMembership number is purely derivable from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, so \u2014 like the existing `displayName` and `initials` \u2014 it belongs as a computed response field rather than a stored column or a creation-pipeline step (which are reserved for values that depend on *other* owners or request state, like `customerCode`, `householdId`, and `namesakeCount`).\n\nTwo small changes, reusing the established pattern:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` gains the field via the generator), documenting the `<customerCode>-M<YY>` format.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` alongside the existing computed fields, plus a single-responsibility `membershipNumber(owner)` default method that formats `customerCode + \"-M\" + last-two-digits-of-registration-year` (zero-padded), returning `null` until both source fields are set.\n\nFor a `2026` registration, `SMI-0007` yields `SMI-0007-M26`, matching the spec example and the test's `registrationDate` year extraction.",
